  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At Le Brusc, in Six-Fours-les-Plages, Bruscain Paddle rents paddleboards (paddle or motorised) and inflatable kayaks and gives beginner lessons, for two months a year, in July and August. It also offers equipment delivery at Le Brusc (corniche des Îles).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to its website, welcoming dogs is the company's specialty: you can paddle or kayak with your dog. The website does not publish prices or detailed rules for dogs: ask by phone on 06 67 30 20 49. At Le Brusc, the lagoon is protected (only kayaks, paddleboards and outrigger canoes are allowed, and according to the tourist office swimming is discouraged in the seagrass beds), so check on site whether your dog can swim.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming to arrange the outing, especially if it's your dog's first time on a paddleboard.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Le Brusc lagoon and the Embiez archipelago are close by.</p>
